When learning about history, I like to visualize when certain events happened relative to other events to better understand the context.<p>I started working on this idea of using AI to take an input topic and generate an interactive timeline of important events within the topic.<p>Some topics to try:<p>&quot;Tell me about the history of space exploration&quot;
&quot;When were important fossils discovered?&quot;
&quot;Show me when all the nintendo consoles were released&quot;<p>For now the generated events must be &quot;known&quot; by the LLM. One idea to improve event generation is to hook the AI up to a Wikipedia MCP server or something.<p>Also interested in adding features like &#x27;expand on this event&#x27; or &#x27;show more events between these two&#x27;<p>Help build it: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;MichaelMilstead&#x2F;timeline-of-everything">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;MichaelMilstead&#x2F;timeline-of-everything</a>
